# Callback / Lifecycle Hooks System

## Purpose

Developers hook into every step of the ReAct loop to stream progress updates to users, log activity, or implement custom abort logic.

## Callbacks by Phase

### Loop-Level
| Callback | When | Receives |
|---|---|---|
| `onLoopStart` | Loop begins | `string $prompt` |
| `onLoopComplete` | Final answer produced | `AgentResponse $response, int $totalIterations` |
| `onMaxIterationsReached` | Limit hit | `AgentResponse $response, int $totalIterations` |

### Iteration-Level
| Callback | When | Receives |
|---|---|---|
| `onIterationStart` | Each iteration begins | `int $iteration` |
| `onIterationEnd` | Each iteration ends | `int $iteration, AgentResponse $response` |

### Thought (LLM Reasoning)
| Callback | When | Receives |
|---|---|---|
| `onBeforeThought` | Before LLM prompt | `string $prompt, int $iteration` |
| `onAfterThought` | After LLM responds | `AgentResponse $response, int $iteration` |

### Action (Tool Execution)
| Callback | When | Receives |
|---|---|---|
| `onBeforeAction` | Before tool call | `string $toolName, array $arguments, int $iteration` |
| `onAfterAction` | After tool returns | `string $toolName, array $arguments, string $result, int $iteration` |

### Observation (Results Fed Back)
| Callback | When | Receives |
|---|---|---|
| `onObservation` | Observation ready | `string $observation, int $iteration` |

## Registration API

```php
$result = (new SalesCoach)
    ->onBeforeAction(function (string $tool, array $args, int $iteration) {
        broadcast(new ToolCallStarted($tool, $args));
    })
    ->onObservation(function (string $observation, int $iteration) {
        broadcast(new ObservationReady($observation));
    })
    ->onLoopComplete(function (AgentResponse $response, int $iterations) {
        logger()->info("Completed in {$iterations} iterations");
    })
    ->reactLoop('Analyze this transcript...');
```

## Rules

- Each `on*` method returns `$this` for fluent chaining
- Callbacks are observers — they MUST NOT alter the loop flow
- Callbacks are optional — loops work identically with zero callbacks registered
